WEBVTT

00:00:02.920 --> 00:00:06.250
Thursday at 11:50 AM,
I was in the middle of proofreading.

00:00:06.540 --> 00:00:10.040
I was at my desk like usual when a call came in
from the property manager of my apartment.

00:00:11.750 --> 00:00:14.170
Ah, Matsukata-san, I'm glad you made it!

00:00:14.750 --> 00:00:17.330
She informed me of a potential leak
in the apartment above mine.

00:00:17.500 --> 00:00:18.500
I rushed home.

00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:22.920
I was just passing by the 7th floor
when I noticed water flowing into the hallway.

00:00:22.920 --> 00:00:24.590
It was really that bad?

00:00:24.580 --> 00:00:28.370
When I saw it, I started wondering if it was
leaking down into your apartment, Matsukata-san.

00:00:43.630 --> 00:00:46.010
Rain can fall, even through a ceiling.

00:00:46.580 --> 00:00:49.620
I suppose nothing is certain in this world...

00:01:09.630 --> 00:01:14.010
Shigoto dekiru otoko sore ga kanojo no konomi
A man who can work, that's the type she likes

00:01:15.380 --> 00:01:18.300
Kiai irete tsutometa no daga
I psyched myself up and got down to business

00:01:18.290 --> 00:01:20.870
Isogashii wa tsuman nai wa
But I'm always so busy and so bored

00:01:21.080 --> 00:01:25.540
Ima no kaisha kanari level takai hou dashi
The company I work at now is pretty high level

00:01:26.960 --> 00:01:29.710
Oyaji garami no kone mo aru kara
And my dad has a lot of connections there

00:01:29.880 --> 00:01:31.880
Yameru wakya nai shi
So there's no way I can quit

00:01:44.540 --> 00:01:50.290
Itsumo boku wa hitori kiri
I'm always all by myself

00:01:50.290 --> 00:01:55.500
Furo ni haitte neru dake
I just take a bath and fall asleep

00:01:55.670 --> 00:02:00.880
Nagameru koto sae dekinai
I can't even take the time to admire

00:02:01.170 --> 00:02:07.340
Kimi no kami o aruku sugata o
Your hair or the way you walk

00:02:07.540 --> 00:02:12.620
Nerukoto shika dekinai
If all I can do is sleep

00:02:13.210 --> 00:02:18.920
Semete yume no naka de demo
Then at least in my dreams

00:02:18.920 --> 00:02:20.920
Kimi ni aitai
I want to see you

00:02:23.580 --> 00:02:27.960
Nevertheless, Hataraki Man

00:02:28.830 --> 00:02:31.160
I need to get to Gokokuji. As fast as you can!

00:02:33.000 --> 00:02:36.710
I made some temporary fixes at the apartment
and headed back to the office.

00:02:37.080 --> 00:02:39.330
Oh, I forgot to call the office and let them know!

00:02:42.710 --> 00:02:44.750
My battery is dead?!

00:02:46.920 --> 00:02:48.590
On top of that, rush hour?!

00:02:49.540 --> 00:02:51.040
I'm such an idiot...

00:02:51.210 --> 00:02:53.380
I shouldn't have relied on the expressway...

00:02:54.130 --> 00:02:56.960
I told you this was due at 3 PM,
so why are you here now?

00:02:57.130 --> 00:02:58.590
Everyone was waiting.

00:02:58.790 --> 00:02:59.710
Right...

00:03:00.170 --> 00:03:03.000
If you're going to be late, then be late,
but you have to let me know ahead of time.

00:03:03.210 --> 00:03:04.670
I'm very sorry.

00:03:10.670 --> 00:03:12.250
Proofread...

00:03:12.750 --> 00:03:13.750
Matsukata.

00:03:14.130 --> 00:03:17.630
Those articles we discussed about
Hoshikawa and Chinese diplomatic relations...

00:03:17.630 --> 00:03:18.760
They're finished, right?

00:03:19.580 --> 00:03:22.710
Because they're going STRAIGHT into next issue.
Sorry to keep you waiting.

00:03:24.540 --> 00:03:26.500
Th-those were...

00:03:27.500 --> 00:03:30.330
I had gathered the evidence and interviews
for those articles 3 months ago.

00:03:30.330 --> 00:03:32.460
"Behind the Curtain of Chinese-Japanese Relations."

00:03:32.460 --> 00:03:38.090
And also, "Following the Missing Money: Former
Minister Hoshikawa's History in Health and Welfare."

00:03:38.080 --> 00:03:39.540
They were all ready to go.

00:03:40.540 --> 00:03:43.370
And of course... both of them
were inside this computer.

00:03:44.040 --> 00:03:46.670
I still have the interviews
and other documents on file, but...

00:03:48.210 --> 00:03:53.290
At this point, I have no willpower left to clean the
apartment... so may I please stay with you tonight?

00:03:53.540 --> 00:03:55.250
No, I'll come to you.

00:03:55.580 --> 00:03:58.250
If we don't get your place cleaned tonight,
it will ruin your floor.

00:04:00.210 --> 00:04:01.250
Call time:
2 minutes 31 seconds

00:04:02.500 --> 00:04:06.830
Our first call in over two weeks...
and that's all we talk about.

00:04:07.330 --> 00:04:08.830
Call time:
2 minutes 31 seconds

00:04:16.710 --> 00:04:20.500
The fact that the leak is mainly coming
from above your sink probably means

00:04:20.500 --> 00:04:23.250
this pipe in the apartment above broke,
or part of the connector joint came loose.

00:04:23.540 --> 00:04:24.420
Yeah...

00:04:24.630 --> 00:04:26.800
Tomorrow the company responsible for repairs
will send their staff to check it out.

00:04:27.290 --> 00:04:29.620
It'll be okay, they should compensate you
for all the damage.

00:04:33.000 --> 00:04:34.210
Let's put down some towels.

00:04:35.130 --> 00:04:35.800
Hiro.

00:04:37.960 --> 00:04:39.340
Let's put down some towels.

00:04:39.330 --> 00:04:40.580
Ah... okay.

00:04:42.960 --> 00:04:46.090
It's been so long since I've seen Shinji
in my apartment...

00:04:49.040 --> 00:04:52.250
When did it reach the point that we stopped
seeing each other unless we specifically set a date?

00:04:53.790 --> 00:04:55.040
How's your new job in sales?

00:04:56.500 --> 00:04:59.040
Well, I'm just as busy as I was before.

00:04:59.170 --> 00:05:00.130
How about you, Hiro?

00:05:01.040 --> 00:05:04.960
When did our conversations
become so aimless and superficial?

00:05:06.580 --> 00:05:08.790
I... got reprimanded today.

00:05:08.790 --> 00:05:09.750
Why is that?

00:05:10.170 --> 00:05:13.250
I suddenly left in the middle of proofreading
to come home, remember?

00:05:13.580 --> 00:05:17.370
On top of that, my phone's battery died
so I couldn't call the office,

00:05:17.380 --> 00:05:19.340
and my taxi got stuck in rush hour.

00:05:19.460 --> 00:05:21.710
You didn't tell them about the apartment leak?

00:05:22.130 --> 00:05:23.920
That has nothing to do with work.

00:05:25.420 --> 00:05:27.960
I'm oddly defensive about explaining
my personal circumstances.

00:05:28.170 --> 00:05:32.630
Because of people like Kaji-san and Yumi-chan,
who can easily explain their way out of anything.

00:05:33.670 --> 00:05:36.300
But... that's not something
I can make him understand.

00:05:36.750 --> 00:05:38.960
I don't think you have to be that strict about it.

00:05:41.130 --> 00:05:42.630
I mean, you're a lady, so-

00:05:49.420 --> 00:05:51.210
This is exactly why I said
I wanted to stay at your place!

00:05:51.630 --> 00:05:52.510
I'm tired of dealing with it!

00:05:53.330 --> 00:05:56.120
But if we just leave it like this today
then things will just be worse later...

00:05:56.330 --> 00:05:57.540
like the bed and the computer!

00:05:57.830 --> 00:06:00.620
Not to mention all my clothes!

00:06:00.630 --> 00:06:02.760
What should I do?! I can't take this!

00:06:02.750 --> 00:06:03.830
Calm down, Hiro!

00:06:03.830 --> 00:06:05.910
I just want it to all go away!

00:06:09.830 --> 00:06:12.210
Shinji Yamashiro (30)
Sales Employee at a Major Construction Contractor

00:06:12.500 --> 00:06:17.630
When I'm with her...
I can't say I feel relaxed, but rather...

00:06:17.630 --> 00:06:21.880
although I want to see her, it's rough to be
in the same room together... is how I feel, lately.

00:06:23.540 --> 00:06:25.790
Come on, I'm begging you, Yamashiro-san!

00:06:26.170 --> 00:06:29.130
Yesterday I couldn't come up
with anything to talk about!

00:06:29.290 --> 00:06:31.710
What's this? You bailed during the party last night?

00:06:31.710 --> 00:06:35.840
Ah, not exactly. Um... a friend called me
to help with a leak in their apartment.

00:06:35.830 --> 00:06:37.580
That's the most made-up excuse I've ever heard!

00:06:37.580 --> 00:06:40.370
No, really! Our company
built the apartment building.

00:06:40.630 --> 00:06:42.380
So, I thought it would be best
to see the damage for myself.

00:06:42.790 --> 00:06:46.290
I see. In the end, you still
haven't given up being a foreman.

00:06:46.290 --> 00:06:47.460
I get it.

00:06:47.460 --> 00:06:48.670
That's not the real reason!

00:06:49.130 --> 00:06:51.420
The "friend" is actually his girlfriend, right?

00:06:51.830 --> 00:06:52.830
Where's she live?

00:06:52.830 --> 00:06:55.370
In Nakame. The Typose building
in Nakameguro to be specific.

00:06:55.670 --> 00:06:58.420
Ah, Moriyama-san was the foreman
in charge of that one.

00:06:58.580 --> 00:07:02.120
He must be headed over there soon. He'll definitely
get a call about it since it's his responsibility.

00:07:02.920 --> 00:07:04.920
Hold on a minute, isn't Moriyama-san...?

00:07:05.250 --> 00:07:06.040
Yeah.

00:07:06.250 --> 00:07:07.460
He was my instructor.

00:07:11.750 --> 00:07:14.380
Oh! Long time, no talk. What're you up to?

00:07:14.710 --> 00:07:17.090
Yeah. I'm heading there now.

00:07:17.460 --> 00:07:19.130
What's that? Your friend?

00:07:19.290 --> 00:07:23.290
Yes. Yesterday, I actually took a look
at the apartment below the one that leaked.

00:07:23.670 --> 00:07:27.000
I noticed the straight pipe below the sink
wasn't properly put into place with supports,

00:07:27.420 --> 00:07:30.340
so I think it's likely the connector joint
on the upper floor came loose.

00:07:31.830 --> 00:07:33.160
Huh? Did I say something weird?

00:07:33.330 --> 00:07:37.040
Why do you sound so excited about it?
I thought you were in sales now.

00:07:38.170 --> 00:07:39.960
Do I really sound excited?

00:07:40.290 --> 00:07:42.920
Yes. Please help her out.

00:07:52.170 --> 00:07:55.130
Looks like the entire ceiling
and all the wallpaper will need redoing.

00:07:55.540 --> 00:07:57.080
What should we do with the floor?

00:07:57.080 --> 00:07:58.710
If you have a preference...

00:07:58.710 --> 00:08:00.750
That will take a lot of time, right?

00:08:00.750 --> 00:08:03.580
Well... we'd have you choose
a few days that work best...

00:08:03.920 --> 00:08:06.500
I can't afford to take time off for that.

00:08:06.500 --> 00:08:07.830
Then just leave it as-is.

00:08:09.420 --> 00:08:12.710
If possible I'd like the ceiling
and wallpaper to be done in one day...

00:08:12.710 --> 00:08:15.380
Unfortunately, it will take longer than just one day.

00:08:15.380 --> 00:08:17.460
I'd estimate two days at the least.

00:08:17.670 --> 00:08:20.750
Huh?! Then just do the ceiling by itself.

00:08:20.960 --> 00:08:23.540
I have to get going really soon.

00:08:23.540 --> 00:08:24.830
Then, how about this?

00:08:25.540 --> 00:08:28.250
We'll just have you check the work in the mornings,

00:08:28.250 --> 00:08:31.250
and in the evenings,
the manager can lock everything up.

00:08:31.250 --> 00:08:33.290
Sure, I can handle that.

00:08:34.170 --> 00:08:38.000
It's depressing to come home from a day of work
to a ruined apartment, don't you think?

00:08:39.540 --> 00:08:41.710
N-no... but...

00:08:42.080 --> 00:08:46.460
Well... I heard that you're an acquaintance
of Yamashiro, who works at our company.

00:08:47.170 --> 00:08:49.590
Actually, I was his direct instructor when he started.

00:08:49.790 --> 00:08:52.080
He called me earlier to tell me about you.

00:08:53.000 --> 00:08:55.500
Shinji's... instructor?

00:08:56.130 --> 00:08:59.300
Countdown to the 2002 FIFA World Cup
in Japan and Korea
183 Days Remaining

00:08:59.290 --> 00:09:00.920
Countdown to the 2002
FIFA World Cup
in Japan and Korea
183 Days Remaining

00:09:02.290 --> 00:09:04.120
Shinji! Did they assign you
to a construction site yet?

00:09:04.380 --> 00:09:07.050
They did, they did! An entertainment hall site.

00:09:07.210 --> 00:09:08.710
An entertainment hall?!

00:09:08.710 --> 00:09:10.670
Congrats! That's just what you wanted!

00:09:10.670 --> 00:09:15.550
Yeah, and my instructor is going
to be this man named Moriyama-san.

00:09:15.710 --> 00:09:17.040
He's really amazing!

00:09:17.710 --> 00:09:19.420
Really? What kind of person is he?

00:09:21.210 --> 00:09:24.000
Note: A famous Japanese actor known for his role as the blind swordsman,
"Zatoichi."
Imagine if you took the actor Shintaro Katsu
and watered him down with milk.

00:09:27.080 --> 00:09:28.410
What kind of description is that?

00:09:28.420 --> 00:09:31.880
Well he looks really intimidating,
but he loves cute character merchandise!

00:09:32.790 --> 00:09:33.830
That's hilarious!

00:09:35.290 --> 00:09:36.790
I'd love to meet him.

00:09:40.210 --> 00:09:42.670
He loves cute character merchandise...

00:09:44.790 --> 00:09:47.540
The actor Shintaro Katsu watered down with milk...

00:09:48.710 --> 00:09:51.460
Are you... Moriyama-san?

00:09:51.460 --> 00:09:52.090
Yes.

00:09:52.250 --> 00:09:53.540
I know you!

00:09:53.540 --> 00:09:56.250
Wow! It's true, you have
a cute rabbit strap on your phone!

00:09:58.080 --> 00:10:01.580
For 2 years after he joined that company,
this guy was all Shinji would talk about.

00:10:02.790 --> 00:10:05.670
I'm sorry, I've just heard so much about you.

00:10:06.040 --> 00:10:10.120
Well, Yamashiro and I have
about 2 years of history together.

00:10:10.130 --> 00:10:11.840
Although he's working in our sales division now.

00:10:12.130 --> 00:10:15.960
That's pretty rare, a transfer from site work to sales.

00:10:17.380 --> 00:10:19.340
He's working fairly hard at it.

00:10:19.580 --> 00:10:22.460
Well then, I'll be back again with my crew.

00:10:22.460 --> 00:10:23.540
On Sunday.

00:10:26.710 --> 00:10:29.040
Thank you for taking care of all this.

00:10:29.040 --> 00:10:30.920
Of course, see you again.

00:10:30.920 --> 00:10:33.420
Ah... thank you very much!

00:10:43.000 --> 00:10:47.380
Now that I think about it, since he moved to sales,
he never talks about work anymore.

00:10:53.250 --> 00:10:55.630
Gotansha Publishing

00:10:55.750 --> 00:10:58.380
This is bad! Mogi-sensei's plane...

00:10:58.380 --> 00:10:59.550
they're saying it crashed!

00:11:00.250 --> 00:11:03.500
The plane Mogi-sensei was riding on
just crashed near the Himalayas!

00:11:03.500 --> 00:11:06.540
It was just reported on the Fuji Network home page!

00:11:08.960 --> 00:11:10.210
Matsukata.

00:11:10.210 --> 00:11:12.130
You've got some free time, right?

00:11:12.130 --> 00:11:14.960
I need 3 pages, the theme
is tax increases. By tomorrow!

00:11:14.960 --> 00:11:15.840
Huh?!

00:11:15.830 --> 00:11:17.580
Are you crazy, Editor-in-Chief?

00:11:18.130 --> 00:11:21.800
But Narita said you're the only one
with enough time to get it done.

00:11:22.250 --> 00:11:25.130
Everyone's been rattled
by the news about Mogi-sensei, too.

00:11:25.330 --> 00:11:27.870
I'm also pretty rattled by it, you know...

00:11:28.880 --> 00:11:31.420
I should have just told them about
what happened from the beginning.

00:11:31.790 --> 00:11:33.750
Now I'm just having a pity party for myself.

00:11:34.500 --> 00:11:36.580
Fine. I'll do it.

00:11:39.710 --> 00:11:45.130
If I think that simply admitting "I can't" do something
is giving up, then I just have to do it.

00:11:46.250 --> 00:11:48.670
I want to become a real adult.

00:11:48.920 --> 00:11:49.800
Hey!

00:11:49.790 --> 00:11:51.080
Who said you could eat in here?

00:11:51.210 --> 00:11:53.040
I mean, I'm hungry...

00:11:53.630 --> 00:11:56.170
And here I was ready to break out
some wine for us...

00:11:56.380 --> 00:11:58.010
Huh? I don't need any.

00:11:58.000 --> 00:11:59.210
I have work to do.

00:11:59.500 --> 00:12:00.830
You drink it, Masami.

00:12:03.880 --> 00:12:04.590
Here.

00:12:04.580 --> 00:12:05.870
Oh, thank you.

00:12:06.210 --> 00:12:08.500
You're as selfish as always.

00:12:08.500 --> 00:12:10.500
Waltzing into someone else's place to do your work.

00:12:10.750 --> 00:12:12.210
Shinji has it rough.

00:12:12.710 --> 00:12:13.960
Yeah, maybe.

00:12:16.790 --> 00:12:20.620
I might just be imagining it, but our conversations
have become really dull lately.

00:12:20.880 --> 00:12:25.710
Lovers don't need stimulating conversation when
they can just pinch each other's nipples instead!

00:12:26.580 --> 00:12:28.710
We haven't been pinching at all, either.

00:12:30.790 --> 00:12:32.920
We've been less and less physical...

00:12:33.670 --> 00:12:36.420
and feelings about work suddenly seem to differ.

00:12:36.830 --> 00:12:37.870
Now this...

00:12:39.290 --> 00:12:43.170
More importantly, why did you even come here
when you could be staying with Shinji?

00:12:43.580 --> 00:12:44.410
I'm not sure...

00:12:46.750 --> 00:12:51.420
It's too bad... On the surface,
you two seem like the perfect couple.

00:12:57.250 --> 00:12:58.460
Thank you for coming!

00:13:02.960 --> 00:13:04.880
Alright, I'm headed this way.

00:13:04.880 --> 00:13:05.920
I'll see you tomorrow.

00:13:05.920 --> 00:13:07.340
Oh, good work today.

00:13:13.080 --> 00:13:15.540
WEEKLY JIDAI SPECIAL ISSUE
THE FIFTY SAMURAI

00:13:20.580 --> 00:13:25.790
Well, I'm working on a special issue
called "The Fifty Samurai," but...

00:13:23.750 --> 00:13:26.750
Yasuyuki Mimura

00:13:44.130 --> 00:13:49.380
It's too bad... On the surface,
you two seem like the perfect couple.

00:13:50.830 --> 00:13:54.080
I feel like the strings keeping us together
are slowly being cut away.

00:13:54.380 --> 00:13:59.510
Love is something

00:13:54.380 --> 00:13:56.920
One after the other...

00:13:57.710 --> 00:14:01.590
Those thin strings snap and arc
through the air into the darkness.

00:14:00.670 --> 00:14:05.710
Known through tears

00:14:05.710 --> 00:14:07.340
It looks like a totally different room...

00:14:07.080 --> 00:14:12.250
And joy is

00:14:07.580 --> 00:14:09.580
We'll have it back to normal real soon.

00:14:10.000 --> 00:14:10.670
Okay.

00:14:13.420 --> 00:14:21.420
The light that illuminates us

00:14:16.210 --> 00:14:20.710
Just one board and one sheet of wallpaper
hides away all the cold steel surrounding this room.

00:14:21.830 --> 00:14:25.830
Even if they put it back to normal,
I've already seen the truth that lies behind it.

00:14:25.920 --> 00:14:30.380
See, just take a look

00:14:26.540 --> 00:14:30.370
Behind the facade
of a warm and inviting apartment...

00:14:32.420 --> 00:14:37.960
You can hear the voices of the children

00:14:38.630 --> 00:14:43.510
In this same old town

00:14:45.000 --> 00:14:55.880
The view around us will oblige our past and future

00:14:55.580 --> 00:14:56.910
We're done with the work for today.

00:14:56.920 --> 00:14:58.250
Thank you very much.

00:14:57.670 --> 00:15:02.250
Once again someone is singing tonight

00:15:03.750 --> 00:15:08.540
The stars light up the night sky

00:15:07.460 --> 00:15:09.960
Okay... just a little bit left.

00:15:11.500 --> 00:15:12.380
Who's there?!

00:15:18.000 --> 00:15:19.080
Shinji!

00:15:19.080 --> 00:15:21.710
Man, this work looks absolutely beautiful!

00:15:21.710 --> 00:15:23.750
Moriyama-san really is the best in the business!

00:15:23.750 --> 00:15:25.920
Uh, no, this was all done by the workers...

00:15:28.580 --> 00:15:31.460
WORKERS ONLY DO THEIR BEST WHEN
THEY WORK UNDER SOMEONE THEY RESPECT!

00:15:31.630 --> 00:15:33.800
I can hear you! Please don't yell!

00:15:33.920 --> 00:15:35.250
It's 2 in the morning!

00:15:35.830 --> 00:15:40.080
It's all cleaned up now... that's good... so good...

00:15:40.080 --> 00:15:40.960
Ah, be careful!

00:15:41.330 --> 00:15:42.620
What happened?!

00:15:42.830 --> 00:15:46.120
It's Sunday but you're wearing
a suit and absolutely wasted...

00:15:46.250 --> 00:15:47.330
I've never seen you like this.

00:15:47.750 --> 00:15:49.420
I was working.

00:15:50.790 --> 00:15:52.710
GOING OUT FOR DRINKS IS AN IMPORTANT PART
OF BEING A SALESMAN!

00:15:52.710 --> 00:15:54.460
EVEN ON SUNDAYS, IT'S A MUST!

00:15:54.460 --> 00:15:56.540
Shh! You don't have to yell!

00:16:02.500 --> 00:16:06.710
Not everybody has a job where
they just create things like you do, Hiro...

00:16:08.880 --> 00:16:12.510
It's not as if I'm actually creating anything new.

00:16:12.880 --> 00:16:17.460
I just pick up pieces of information
and pass them along...

00:16:18.040 --> 00:16:19.670
Then tell me why!

00:16:21.290 --> 00:16:24.330
Why do you always take it so damn far?!

00:16:27.330 --> 00:16:29.500
People suffer when you set the bar so high!

00:16:29.500 --> 00:16:31.710
Even though they know it's not your fault!

00:16:33.460 --> 00:16:35.920
I can't... be at your level.

00:16:37.420 --> 00:16:39.090
When I look at you, Hiro,

00:16:39.080 --> 00:16:42.500
all I can do is be frustrated
with how incapable I am!

00:16:43.460 --> 00:16:44.790
I... never intended...

00:16:44.790 --> 00:16:46.370
IT'S NOT YOUR FAULT, HIRO!

00:16:47.670 --> 00:16:49.300
It's not your fault, Hiro...

00:16:51.000 --> 00:16:52.540
It's not your fault, Hiro.

00:16:53.170 --> 00:16:54.250
We should...

00:16:55.080 --> 00:16:57.000
just break up.

00:16:58.290 --> 00:17:00.170
Nothing is certain in this world.

00:17:01.630 --> 00:17:03.460
Yeah... you're right.

00:17:09.750 --> 00:17:13.000
Our time together was always short,
so we avoided voicing any complaints.

00:17:14.920 --> 00:17:20.130
Explaining the details of our lives became a pain, so
we gradually stopped sharing them with each other.

00:17:27.920 --> 00:17:29.880
February 19th Issue of JIDAI
"Behind the Curtain
of Chinese-Japanese Relations"

00:17:32.330 --> 00:17:33.660
I'm finished...

00:17:40.420 --> 00:17:41.920
Can I send this to print now?

00:17:41.920 --> 00:17:43.460
Whoa! You're so fast!

00:17:46.290 --> 00:17:48.000
Matsukata, what's wrong?

00:17:48.420 --> 00:17:49.710
You look like a statue.

00:17:50.960 --> 00:17:54.540
Huh? No, nothing's wrong.

00:17:54.960 --> 00:17:57.540
I wonder what happened...
It's rare to see her like that.

00:17:57.540 --> 00:18:01.000
I bet she's still thinking about the accident
that happened yesterday.

00:18:02.330 --> 00:18:03.460
Senpai!

00:18:06.670 --> 00:18:08.960
If you've got puffy eyes
from a lack of sleep, use these!

00:18:08.960 --> 00:18:10.340
Cold spoons!

00:18:10.880 --> 00:18:11.800
Ouch...

00:18:13.040 --> 00:18:14.540
Time for the meeting.

00:18:20.790 --> 00:18:25.710
Why is it that despite everything that's happened...
I still insist on working?

00:18:29.380 --> 00:18:30.460
Kaji-san!

00:18:30.460 --> 00:18:32.210
Apparently Mogi-sensei is alive!

00:18:33.580 --> 00:18:34.960
He was supposed to be on that plane,

00:18:34.960 --> 00:18:37.500
but his secretary came down with
a fever so they didn't make it!

00:18:37.500 --> 00:18:40.170
Instead they ended up going
to a hospital in Bangkok,

00:18:40.330 --> 00:18:42.790
which is why they weren't able
to get a hold of us until now!

00:18:42.790 --> 00:18:44.170
What a relief!

00:18:45.380 --> 00:18:47.960
So these kinds of crazy coincidences
really do happen.

00:18:47.960 --> 00:18:51.090
Yeah, I remember how pale everyone looked
after that call yesterday.

00:18:51.250 --> 00:18:53.420
He really can't be more lucky than that!

00:18:54.130 --> 00:18:55.010
Matsukata.

00:18:56.170 --> 00:19:00.130
Just because you focused on your job,
doesn't mean it caused harm. Okay?

00:19:03.790 --> 00:19:07.330
It'll definitely play a role
the next time you fall in love.

00:19:27.630 --> 00:19:29.170
Sugawara-san...?

00:19:30.960 --> 00:19:31.630
Natto
Roll
Natto
Roll

00:19:32.670 --> 00:19:34.300
Natto rolls...?

00:19:51.750 --> 00:19:52.880
Thanks for getting these...

00:20:00.080 --> 00:20:02.710
It's because you like it, this job.

00:20:03.080 --> 00:20:04.040
Huh?

00:20:05.420 --> 00:20:10.130
Why is it that despite everything that's happened...
I still insist on working?

00:20:36.210 --> 00:20:37.460
Shangri-la

00:20:37.670 --> 00:20:42.800
Yume no naka de sae umaku waraenai kimi no koto
Even in my dreams you can't manage a proper smile

00:20:42.790 --> 00:20:48.170
Dame na hitotte shikari nagara aishiteitai
I just want to chide and love a hopeless person like you

00:20:47.330 --> 00:20:50.290
Weekly JIDAI February 12th Issue

00:20:51.000 --> 00:20:54.960
Keitai denwa o kawa ni otoshita yo
I dropped my cell phone in the river

00:20:54.960 --> 00:20:58.670
Sasabune no youni nagaretetta yo
It got swept away just like a toy boat

00:20:58.670 --> 00:21:04.210
Ahh... ahh...

00:21:06.040 --> 00:21:09.500
Weekly JIDAI February 12th Issue
Kimi o omouto kyou mo nemurenai
Today I thought about you and now I can't sleep

00:21:09.880 --> 00:21:13.460
Bokura doko he mukaouka
Where shall we go?

00:21:13.460 --> 00:21:18.630
Ahh... ahh...

00:21:20.830 --> 00:21:22.290
Shangri-la

00:21:22.290 --> 00:21:26.170
Shiawasedatte sakende kureyo
Let me hear you shout "I'm happy!"

00:21:26.170 --> 00:21:30.630
Ijippari na kimi no nakigao misete kureyo
Let me see the tears underneath your tough exterior

00:21:30.630 --> 00:21:32.050
Shangri-la

00:21:32.210 --> 00:21:37.170
Kimi o omouto kyou mo nemurenai boku no koto
Today I thought about you and now I can't sleep

00:21:37.170 --> 00:21:42.500
Dame na hitotte shikarinagara ashitekure
Please chide and love a hopeless person like me

00:21:38.670 --> 00:21:39.710
Gimme JIDAI.

00:21:39.710 --> 00:21:41.250
That'll be 340 yen.

00:21:52.580 --> 00:21:53.210
Yes?

00:21:53.670 --> 00:21:57.250
Today, the police are going to execute a search
warrant on Former Minister Hoshikawa's house.

00:21:59.540 --> 00:22:00.670
Can you get there?

00:22:00.670 --> 00:22:02.840
I'm in Shibuya now, so I can be there in no time.

00:22:02.830 --> 00:22:03.460
Great!

00:22:04.670 --> 00:22:06.960
Sugawara is already en route,
so rendezvous with him there.

00:22:07.210 --> 00:22:08.040
Yessir!

00:22:10.040 --> 00:22:11.870
All of the things I've lost from doing this job...

00:22:13.830 --> 00:22:15.580
...some nights I cry over them.

00:22:15.920 --> 00:22:16.590
But...

00:22:17.380 --> 00:22:18.340
Taxi!

00:22:23.000 --> 00:22:24.790
There are also mornings
when I feel this job is what truly...

00:22:25.790 --> 00:22:26.830
...liberates me.
